## 5. How to Choose the Right Wedding Fabric

Selecting fabric requires more than choosing a beautiful colour.

Consider these five factors:

| Factor | Why It Matters |
|---|---|
| Fabric weight | Influences comfort and garment structure |
| Drape | Determines how the garment falls |
| Embroidery | Affects appearance, stitching, and maintenance |
| Transparency | Helps determine lining requirements |
| Season | Influences comfort and fabric suitability |

A lightweight georgette may be ideal for a flowing outfit, while a structured brocade may be more suitable for a tailored jacket.

The best choice depends on the intended garment, occasion, and personal preference.

